# Neo Vocoder parameters (docs/specs/neo-vocoder.md). The order changes only with a version (machines.md §3.2): songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoVocoder
namespace NeoBuzz.Vocoder
class NeoVocoderMachine
tracks 8
summary Channel vocoder. The main input is the modulator (a voice, drums, anything); its spectral shape, measured in 8 to 40 log-spaced bands, is imposed on a carrier: the machine's own 8-voice synth (saw and pulse with a noise blend, detune, glide and an envelope) played by notes and chords, white noise, or any machine wired into the sidechain (input 2). Each band is a 4th-order band-pass on the modulator and on the carrier; attack and release followers, a formant shift of plus or minus 12 semitones, the modulator's highs passed through for clear consonants, a freeze of the band levels, a stereo spread of odd and even bands, Mix and Amount. Zero latency. Use it for robot and choir voices, talking pads, rhythmic textures from a drum loop and any sound made to speak.

group Carrier
Carrier     "Carrier"        0 2 0       enum Synth Sidechain Noise                         | What the bands are cut from: the synth (played by notes), the sidechain input (input 2), or noise
    how Chooses the carrier: the built-in synth played by notes, any machine wired into the sidechain (input 2), or white noise.
    sound Synth gives a pitched robot or choir, the sidechain makes any sound speak, noise gives a whisper.
Wave        "Wave"           0 1000 0    pct                                                | Synth waveform: 0 % saw, 100 % pulse (square)
    how Blends the synth's oscillators from a saw (all harmonics) to a pulse (odd harmonics).
    sound A saw is bright and buzzy and clearest as speech, a pulse is hollow and reedy.
Noise       "Noise blend"    0 1000 50   pct                                                | Synth: noise mixed into the tone, 0 to 100 %
    how Crossfades the synth's tone toward noise that follows each note's envelope.
    sound A little noise makes the consonants breathy; all of it is a whispered chord.
Detune      "Detune"         0 1000 200  lin 0 50 cents 1                                   | Synth: the two oscillators of each voice are detuned by this much (and spread left and right)
    how Detunes the two oscillators of every voice apart by this many cents and spreads them across the stereo field.
    sound More detune makes a wider, chorused carrier; zero is one steady, centred tone.
Glide       "Glide"          0 1000 0    pow 0 1000 2 ms 0                                  | Synth: time for a new note to glide from the last one; 0 is off
    how Sets how long a note takes to slide from the previous pitch to its own.
    sound Glide makes the voice swoop between notes like a singer or a talk box.
SynAttack   "Synth attack"   0 1000 220  exp 1 2000 ms 0                                   | Synth amplitude envelope: attack
    how Sets how long each synth note takes to rise to full level.
    sound Short attacks make a spoken, percussive voice; long ones swell in like a pad.
SynDecay    "Synth decay"    0 1000 500  exp 5 5000 ms 0                                    | Synth amplitude envelope: decay to the sustain level
    how Sets how long the level takes to fall from the peak to the sustain level.
    sound It shapes the start of a held note; with sustain at 100 % it does nothing.
SynSustain  "Synth sustain"  0 1000 1000 pct                                                | Synth amplitude envelope: sustain level while the note is held
    how Sets the level a held note rests at after the decay.
    sound At 100 % a held note stays full; lower values make a note die away while it is held.
SynRelease  "Synth release"  0 1000 450  exp 5 5000 ms 0                                    | Synth amplitude envelope: release after the note ends
    how Sets how long a note takes to fade out after its key is up.
    sound Short releases stop with the word; long ones let a chord ring on under the next syllable.
group Bands
Bands       "Bands"          0 32 8      int 8                                              | Number of filter bands, 8 to 40
    how Sets how many band-pass filters cut up the spectrum, from 8 to 40.
    sound Few bands give the classic robot with little detail; many bands keep more of the words.
Low         "Low"            0 1000 301  exp 50 500 Hz 0                                    | Centre of the lowest band, 50 to 500 Hz
    how Sets the centre frequency of the lowest band, from 50 to 500 Hz.
    sound Lower values keep more body of the voice; higher values drop the lows out.
High        "High"           0 1000 667  exp 2000 16000 Hz 0                                | Centre of the highest band, 2 to 16 kHz
    how Sets the centre frequency of the highest band, from 2 to 16 kHz.
    sound Higher values keep more air and clarity in the consonants; lower values are darker.
Width       "Width"          0 1000 333  lin 50 200 % 0                                     | Bandwidth of each band as a share of the spacing between bands (Q follows)
    how Sets how wide each band is against the gap to its neighbour: 100 % makes neighbours meet at their half-power points.
    sound Narrow bands are more articulate but thinner; wide bands are smoother and blur the words a little.
group Followers
Attack      "Attack"         0 1000 338  exp 0.5 100 ms 1                                   | Band level follower: time to rise from 10 to 90 % of a step
    how Sets how quickly each band's level follows the modulator when it gets louder.
    sound Fast attacks keep consonants sharp; slow attacks soften and smear them.
Release     "Release"        0 1000 469  exp 5 1000 ms 0                                    | Band level follower: time to fall from 90 to 10 % of a step
    how Sets how slowly each band's level lets go when the modulator gets quieter.
    sound Short releases are crisp and rhythmic, long ones run the syllables together into a wash.
group Voice
Formant     "Formant"        0 24 12     int -12 st signed                                  | Formant shift: the carrier's bands move this many semitones against the modulator's
    how Moves the carrier's bands up or down by up to 12 semitones against the modulator's bands, without changing the carrier's pitch.
    sound Down is a bigger, darker voice, up is a smaller, brighter one.
Sibilance   "Sibilance"      0 1000 350  pct                                                | The modulator's highs above about 5 kHz, passed straight through, 0 to 100 %
    how Mixes in the modulator's own sound above about 5 kHz, unchanged, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound It keeps s, t and f clear, because a pitched carrier cannot make them.
Freeze      "Freeze"         0 1 0       switch                                             | Holds the band levels where they are
    how Holds every band's level at its current value while on.
    sound The carrier keeps the vowel that was spoken when you switched it on, as a held drone.
Spread      "Spread"         0 1000 0    pct                                                | Odd bands to the left, even bands to the right, 0 to 100 %
    how Moves the odd-numbered bands toward the left and the even-numbered bands toward the right, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound At 100 % the voice opens into a wide, shimmering stereo image.
group Output
Mix         "Mix"            0 1000 1000 pct                                                | Dry/wet (the vocoder has no latency, so the dry signal is not delayed)
    how Blends the vocoded sound with the unprocessed modulator.
    sound Lower values keep the original voice in front and lay the carrier under it.
Amount      "Amount"         0 2000 1000 lin 0 200 % 0                                      | Effect strength: 100 % = the settings as shown, 0 % = bypass (bit for bit the input), 200 % = twice the formant shift, sibilance and spread (held to their limits)
    how Scales the formant shift, the sibilance and the spread together. 0 % is bypass, 100 % your settings, 200 % doubles all three up to their limits.
    sound Turn it down to bring the plain vocoder back and then the dry voice, up to push the effect further.
Output      "Output"         0 1000 500  db -24 24                                          | Level of the vocoded sound
    how Sets the level of the vocoded sound in dB, from -24 to +24.
    sound It makes the vocoder louder or quieter without changing the sound.
